    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d157-f1" n="29" xml:id="d157-f1-content">
                <p>For the text of Molotov’s statement under reference here, see Molotov, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Problems of Foreign Policy</hi>, pp. 448–450.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d157-f2" n="30" xml:id="d157-f2-content">
                <p>The document under reference contained the text of Molotov’s statement on the
                    draft Austrian treaty which included a proposal for the establishment of
                    four-power commission to examine all the unagreed clauses in the draft treaty;
                    for the text of Molotov’s statement, see Molotov, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Problems of Foreign Policy</hi>, pp. 451–453.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d157-f3" n="31" xml:id="d157-f3-content">
                <p>It was the understanding of the Department of State that the Council of Foreign
                    Ministers had agreed that September 1, 1947, would be the target date for the
                    reduction of occupation forces in Germany. As a result of a request by the
                    United States, the concluding phrase “as on September 1, 1947” was added to this
                    sentence of the Council’s decision as it was transmitted to the Allied Control
                    Council for Germany in document CFM(47) (M)158, May 10, 1947, <ref
                        target="#pg470">p. 470</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
